# Security headers for static hosts that support the `_headers` convention
# (Netlify, Cloudflare Pages, etc.). GitHub Pages ignores this file.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is intentionally not enforced here yet: the page has
# an inline import map whose hash must be rechecked after any edit. See
# docs/architecture/06-security-and-deployment.md for the Report-Only rollout
# and the exact CSP value.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
